   $q$What is the coach's main claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Colleges should recruit only athletes who played several sports.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Thirteen-year-olds should train for a single sport throughout the year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-claim"},{"text":"Basketball footwork is the best preparation for distance running.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"High school athletes should play two or more sports rather than specialize.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$High school athletes should play two or more sports rather than specialize.$q$, $q$The first paragraph states that athletes "should play at least two sports, and clubs should stop pressuring young players to specialize." The basketball detail is one example, not the claim.$q$, 'draft', 'e1f4f60d-1821-5754-943f-946a14678e33')
