   $q$Why does alternating plate sizes week by week strengthen the study's reasoning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It let students choose which size of plate they wanted each day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It made the results easier for the newsletter to report.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"It allowed the researchers to test twice as many students.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It kept outside changes like exams or weather from favoring one plate size.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It kept outside changes like exams or weather from favoring one plate size.$q$, $q$The passage says alternating spread "changes in season, exam schedules or weather" across both conditions, so they could not explain the difference. Nothing suggests students chose their plate size.$q$, 'draft', '09d51f2c-d3a8-5f97-bdbb-771951c33afd')
