   $q$Why does the petition fail to "settle the question" as the writer claims?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The petition was signed mostly by people who live outside the county.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Popularity shows people want the trail, not that its benefits justify the cost.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The petition contradicts the writer's earlier reasons for the trail.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Two thousand signatures is too few to count as public support.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Popularity shows people want the trail, not that its benefits justify the cost.$q$, $q$A petition measures support, but the commission must still judge whether the trail is worth buying and building, which popularity alone cannot show. Nothing in the passage says who signed it, so the outside-signers choice is unsupported.$q$, 'draft', '4edd66d6-6d04-5b9f-bb6a-423afcb39df1')
