  ('434acafc-7085-548f-a80c-fb50858b8558', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-argument-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$How does the author use the comparison at the twenty sites?$q$, $q$[{"text":"As proof that every volunteer at every site counted accurately.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-text"},{"text":"As direct evidence that volunteer totals closely match trained counts.","is_correct":true},{"text":"As a reason to expand the survey to more than twenty sites.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"As evidence that volunteers count more birds than biologists do.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$As direct evidence that volunteer totals closely match trained counts.$q$, $q$The biologists surveyed the same sites, and volunteer totals "fell within 10 percent" for common species, which tests accuracy directly. The finding is about site totals, not every individual volunteer, and the match held at "nearly every" site.$q$, 'draft', '0418763f-6853-5233-9321-066a2c197ede')
