  ('9d99f8b3-810c-54a7-a8ce-4eabf94ed090', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-argument-evidence'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which conclusion would go beyond the evidence in this passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Rare species are harder for volunteers to detect than common ones.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"consistent-with-evidence"},{"text":"Volunteer counts could fully replace professional bird surveys.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Volunteer counts can track changes in common birds across the region.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"consistent-with-evidence"},{"text":"Combining volunteers and biologists makes good use of both groups.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"consistent-with-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Volunteer counts could fully replace professional bird surveys.$q$, $q$The 30 percent miss rate for rare birds shows volunteers cannot do everything biologists do, so full replacement is unsupported. Tracking common birds is exactly what the twenty-site comparison supports.$q$, 'draft', '0418763f-6853-5233-9321-066a2c197ede')
